cff-version: 1.2.0
message: >-
  If you use SecuraX in your research, please cite it using the metadata
  in this file. See also: https://citation-file-format.github.io/

title: "SecuraX: A Unified Cybersecurity Scanning and Research Platform"

version: 2.0.0
date-released: "2026-07-30"

abstract: >-
  SecuraX is an open-source, self-hosted cybersecurity research platform that
  orchestrates 11 scanner engines (DAST, SAST, Network, SSL/TLS, DNS, Docker,
  WordPress, Dependencies) through a unified Flask REST API and React dashboard.
  The platform implements a multi-dimensional risk scoring engine extending
  CVSS v3.1 with temporal adjustment (CISA KEV integration, known-exploit flags)
  and environmental adjustment (asset criticality, PII exposure, internet-facing
  context). SecuraX is designed for reproducible security research: every scan
  result is stored with full provenance, and the risk engine is versioned so that
  experiments can be reproduced with a specific engine version. The platform
  supports GDPR Art. 32/33, PCI-DSS Req. 6.3.3, ISO 27001 A.14.2, OWASP Top 10
  (2021), and MITRE ATT&CK compliance mapping.

license: MIT

repository-code: "https://github.com/Abdallahbenaicha/SecuraX"

url: "https://securax.vercel.app"

keywords:
  - cybersecurity
  - vulnerability management
  - security scanning
  - CVSS
  - DAST
  - SAST
  - penetration testing
  - risk scoring
  - MITRE ATT&CK
  - OWASP
  - open source security
  - security research platform

